<!doctype html>
<html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1">
<meta name="color-scheme" content="light"><title>Swarm Lab | Evidence before credit</title>
<style>
:root{--paper:#f7f6f3;--ink:#242724;--muted:#686d67;--line:#eaeaea;--green:#346538;--red:#9f2f2d}*{box-sizing:border-box}body{margin:0;background:var(--paper);color:var(--ink);font:16px/1.6 'Helvetica Neue',Arial,sans-serif}main{max-width:1120px;padding:40px 32px 80px;margin:auto}header{display:flex;justify-content:space-between;gap:20px;border-bottom:1px solid var(--line);padding-bottom:22px;font:12px/1.5 monospace;letter-spacing:.07em;text-transform:uppercase}.label{font:11px/1.5 monospace;letter-spacing:.08em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--muted)}h1{font:normal clamp(38px,6vw,70px)/1.03 Georgia,serif;letter-spacing:-.04em;max-width:790px;margin:54px 0 22px}h2{font:normal 32px/1.2 Georgia,serif;letter-spacing:-.025em;margin:8px 0 20px}p{max-width:740px}p.sub{font-size:17px;color:var(--muted);margin-bottom:38px}.notice{padding:13px 17px;background:#fbf3db;font-size:13px;color:#715500;border-left:3px solid #ae9361}.controls{display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:space-between;gap:16px;margin:32px 0 14px}button{font:inherit;border:1px solid #c5c7c1;background:transparent;color:var(--ink);border-radius:4px;padding:8px 15px;cursor:pointer}button:hover{background:#edece6}button:focus-visible,a:focus-visible{outline:3px solid #346538;outline-offset:3px}button.primary{background:var(--ink);color:white;border-color:var(--ink)}button.primary:hover{background:#424742}button:disabled{opacity:.45;cursor:not-allowed}.steps{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(4,1fr);gap:0;border-top:1px solid #d7dad2;border-bottom:1px solid #d7dad2}.step{text-align:left;border:none;border-radius:0;padding:17px 14px;color:var(--muted);border-bottom:3px solid transparent;font-size:14px}.step[aria-current=step]{color:var(--ink);border-bottom-color:var(--ink);background:white}.step small{font:11px monospace;margin-right:9px}.panel{margin-top:24px;padding:32px;background:#fff;border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:8px;min-height:470px;animation:appear .22s ease}.metrics{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,1fr);gap:20px;margin:26px 0}.metric{border-top:1px solid var(--line);padding-top:14px}.metric strong{display:block;font:normal 42px/1.15 Georgia,serif;letter-spacing:-.03em}.metric span{display:block;color:var(--muted);font-size:12px;margin-top:7px}.tag{display:inline-block;padding:3px 8px;font:11px/1.6 monospace;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.04em;background:#edf3ec;color:var(--green);border-radius:3px}.tag.fail{background:#fdebec;color:var(--red)}.muted{color:var(--muted);font-size:13px}.two{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:24px}.proposal{padding:23px;background:#f9f9f8;border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:8px}.proposal h3{margin:10px 0;font-size:18px}.proposal p{font-size:14px}.barrow{display:grid;grid-template-columns:180px 1fr 75px;align-items:center;gap:12px;margin:22px 0;font-size:13px}.track{height:11px;background:#efefea}.fill{height:100%;background:#8b9287}.fill.good{background:#527956}.fill.bad{background:#af827e}.number{text-align:right;font:13px monospace}table{border-collapse:collapse;width:100%;font-size:13px}td,th{padding:12px 8px;text-align:left;border-bottom:1px solid var(--line)}th{font-size:11px;color:var(--muted);font-weight:normal;text-transform:uppercase}td:last-child,th:last-child{text-align:right}.scroll{overflow-x:auto}details{border-bottom:1px solid var(--line);margin:24px 0;padding-bottom:14px}summary{cursor:pointer;font-size:14px}code{font:11px/1.6 monospace;overflow-wrap:anywhere}footer{margin-top:36px;font-size:12px;color:var(--muted);display:flex;justify-content:space-between;gap:20px}a{color:inherit}#counter{font:12px monospace;color:var(--muted)}.source-list{font-size:14px;padding-left:22px}.source-list li{margin:8px 0}.source-list span{color:var(--muted)}@keyframes appear{from{opacity:0;transform:translateY(5px)}to{opacity:1;transform:translateY(0)}}@media(prefers-reduced-motion:reduce){.panel{animation:none}}@media(max-width:640px){main{padding:24px 18px 48px}header{font-size:10px}h1{margin-top:36px}.steps{grid-template-columns:repeat(2,1fr)}.panel{padding:22px 18px}.metrics{gap:10px}.metric strong{font-size:33px}.two{grid-template-columns:1fr}.barrow{grid-template-columns:105px 1fr 62px;gap:8px;font-size:11px}footer{flex-direction:column}.step{font-size:12px;padding:13px 10px}.notice{font-size:12px}}
</style></head><body><main>
<header><span>Swarm Lab / Research infrastructure</span><span>R1 / Offline replay / 04 Oct 2026</span></header>
<h1>An improvement has to survive its evidence.</h1>
<p class="sub">Real run records. Two bounded proposals. One reporting repair earns attribution; a cosmetic shortcut does not.</p>
<div class="notice">Engineering demonstration, not a scientific result. Same-author evaluation. No new model calls, private transcript export or payment.</div>
<div class="controls"><div><button id="play" class="primary">Play replay</button> <button id="next">Next step</button></div><span id="counter">01 / 04</span></div>
<nav class="steps" aria-label="Replay stages"><button class="step" data-step="0"><small>01</small>Ingest evidence</button><button class="step" data-step="1"><small>02</small>Propose a repair</button><button class="step" data-step="2"><small>03</small>Evaluate bundles</button><button class="step" data-step="3"><small>04</small>Record credit</button></nav>
<section id="panel" class="panel" aria-live="polite" aria-atomic="true"></section>
<details><summary>What is, and is not, being demonstrated</summary><p class="muted">The searcher is the current coding agent, shadow/sol-rsi2. Its two proposals are saved artifacts, not fresh LLM output generated by this page. The builder runs a fixed declarative policy language against all 327 frozen episode records. It cannot change outcomes, run arbitrary code or spend money. The reference evaluator was written by the same author, so acceptance is provisional maintenance validation, not independent scientific promotion.</p><p class="muted">The 3 private-pool envelopes are attributed by full approved research-task text, but have no exact join to naming-game policy calls. The 80 public policy-call rows are the first 16 from each of 5 files, not a random sample. The 156 public teammate workflow steps supply provenance context only. These observations are not added together as independent samples or unique provider calls.</p></details>
<details><summary>Per-group attempt accounting</summary><div class="scroll"><table><thead><tr><th>Cell / arm</th><th>Physical</th><th>Invalid</th><th>Logical</th><th>Selected valid</th></tr></thead><tbody id="groups"></tbody></table></div></details>
<footer><span>Source root <code id="root"></code></span><span><a href="../DEMO.md">Demo notes</a> / <a href="summary.json">Measured summary</a> / <a href="credit-ledger.jsonl">Credit receipts</a></span></footer>
</main><script id="replay-data" type="application/json">__REPLAY_DATA__</script><script>
'use strict';
const D=JSON.parse(document.getElementById('replay-data').textContent),S=D.summary,T=S.totals;
const esc=s=>String(s).replace(/[&<>"']/g,c=>({'&':'&amp;','<':'&lt;','>':'&gt;','"':'&quot;',"'":'&#39;'}[c]));
const metric=(n,label)=>`<div class="metric"><strong>${esc(n)}</strong><span>${esc(label)}</span></div>`;
const bar=(label,n,total,kind='')=>`<div class="barrow"><span>${esc(label)}</span><div class="track"><div class="fill ${kind}" style="width:${100*n/total}%"></div></div><span class="number">${n}/${total}</span></div>`;
const views=[()=>`<span class="label">01 / Permissioned metadata, not private text</span><h2>Keep the evidence. Keep the failures.</h2><div class="metrics">${metric(S.envelopes,'validated trace envelopes')}${metric(T.physical_records,'MP3 episode records')}${metric(T.invalid_records,'invalid records preserved')}</div><ul class="source-list"><li><b>${S.source_counts.episode} episode snapshots</b> <span>from all 5 capture-memory-mix MP3 cells.</span></li><li><b>${S.source_counts['policy-call']} public policy-call rows</b> <span>sampled from ${S.policy_call_population.toLocaleString()} recorded rows, five files.</span></li><li><b>${S.source_counts['public-workflow-step']} public workflow steps</b> <span>from dmarz's compositional-safety Q0-011 trace.</span></li><li><b>${S.pool_envelopes} research-session pool envelopes</b> <span>sealed content; no exact game-call join.</span></li></ul><p class="muted">Every public source is content-hashed and re-derived on replay. Missing timing, cost and native attempt identity remain unknown.</p>`,
()=>`<span class="label">02 / Agent-authored, content-addressed proposals</span><h2>Repair the account, not the result.</h2><div class="two"><article class="proposal"><span class="tag">Candidate A</span><h3>Preserve attempt lineage</h3><p>Keep every physical record. Declare last-valid selection, expose failed-first attempts, and compute capture using the same selected population in numerator and denominator.</p><code>all-physical / selected / all / report</code></article><article class="proposal"><span class="tag fail">Candidate B</span><h3>Clamp the rate</h3><p>Clamp a raw-over-selected fraction to one. Keep reporting selected records only, hiding retries and failed attempts. The number looks plausible; the account is still incomplete.</p><code>selected-only / clamp / omit / omit</code></article></div><p class="muted">Both are same-principal maintenance variants. The controller admits only closed policy enums, no arbitrary code. A claimed gain is never a score. Replay consumes saved proposals and makes zero new model calls.</p>`,
()=>`<span class="label">03 / ${S.reporting_groups} groups, 13 checks each</span><h2>The shortcut fails the same test.</h2>${bar('Selected-only baseline',S.baseline.passed,S.baseline.assigned)}${bar('Lineage repair',S.candidates[0].passed,S.candidates[0].assigned,'good')}${bar('Clamp shortcut',S.candidates[1].passed,S.candidates[1].assigned,'bad')}<div class="metrics">${metric(T.first_attempt_valid_records+'/'+T.logical_records,'valid on first observed record')}${metric(T.selected_valid_records+'/'+T.logical_records,'valid after last-valid selection')}${metric(T.superseded_records,'records hidden by selection alone')}</div><p class="muted">The repair passes ${S.candidates[0].passed-S.baseline.passed} additional assertions. The shortcut fails eight check categories in every group. Selected capture is ${T.selected_captured_records}/${T.selected_valid_records}; that does not erase ${T.invalid_records} invalid physical records or establish a scientific effect.</p>`,
()=>`<span class="label">04 / Append-only-style, hash-linked receipts</span><h2>Attribution is not a payment.</h2><p><span class="tag">Lineage repair accepted</span> <span class="tag fail">Clamp shortcut rejected</span></p><div class="metrics">${metric(S.credit_units,'demo attribution units')}${metric('0','rejected-bundle units')}${metric('$0','payable and settled')}</div><table><thead><tr><th>Role</th><th>Principal</th><th>Units</th></tr></thead><tbody>${Object.entries(D.credit_ledger[0].units_by_role).map(([role,n])=>`<tr><td>${esc(role.replace('_bps','').replaceAll('_',' '))}</td><td>shadow</td><td>${n}</td></tr>`).join('')}</tbody></table><p class="muted">The 200/600/100/100 split conserves 1,000 non-transferable units. All roles are related-party maintenance. Every receipt binds the frozen sources, bundle, rubric and measured evaluation. Independent review and any financial settlement remain absent.</p>`];
let index=0,timer=null;
function stop(){clearInterval(timer);timer=null;document.getElementById('play').textContent='Play replay'}
function show(i){index=i;document.getElementById('panel').innerHTML=views[i]();document.querySelectorAll('.step').forEach((b,n)=>{if(n===i)b.setAttribute('aria-current','step');else b.removeAttribute('aria-current')});document.getElementById('counter').textContent=`0${i+1} / 04`;document.getElementById('next').disabled=i===3;if(i===3)stop()}
document.querySelectorAll('.step').forEach(b=>b.addEventListener('click',()=>{stop();show(Number(b.dataset.step))}));
document.getElementById('next').addEventListener('click',()=>{stop();show(Math.min(3,index+1))});
document.getElementById('play').addEventListener('click',()=>{if(timer){stop();return}if(index===3)show(0);document.getElementById('play').textContent='Pause replay';timer=setInterval(()=>show(Math.min(3,index+1)),4000)});
document.getElementById('root').textContent=S.source_root;
document.getElementById('groups').innerHTML=Object.entries(D.groups).map(([g,v])=>`<tr><td>${esc(g.replace('MP_W1_INSIDE_d0.5_',''))}</td><td>${v.physical_records}</td><td>${v.invalid_records}</td><td>${v.logical_records}</td><td>${v.selected_valid_records}</td></tr>`).join('');
show(0);
</script></body></html>
